# What `docker build` leaves out of the image. See HOSTING.md, "Docker".
#
# The server needs the game (index.html, src/, styles/, vendor/, assets/), the
# build tools that make the bundle (tools/), package.json (it is what tells
# Node that src/ is ES modules) and server/ itself. Everything below is either
# history, development tooling, or somebody's data.

# History and CI: tens of megabytes the server never reads.
.git
.github

# Development only. The server has no npm dependencies; node_modules is the
# headless browser the screenshot tools use.
node_modules

# Screenshots from the visual checks.
shots

# Accounts, password hashes and every player's record. A server's data lives
# in a volume, never inside an image that might be pushed somewhere public.
server/data

# Build outputs. The image builds its own from the sources it was given, so a
# stale copy from this working tree can never be the one that gets served.
terraglide.bundle.js
terraglide.html
terraglide-online.html

# Noise.
*.log
.DS_Store
